// Guerrilla Mode on Everon (CfgWorlds >> Eden).
// GENERATED by `PoseidonTools guerrilla scaffold` on 2026-09-02 - a STARTING POINT, not a finished
// campaign. Re-running the tool overwrites this file; pass --keep-zones to
// preserve a hand-edited class Zones block across a re-run.
//
// Zone geometry was derived from worlds\eden.wrp: 4670 road piece(s) and 387
// building(s) were identified by model-path heuristics (Guerrilla::ModelIsRoad
// / ModelIsBuilding), and every elevation below is a real sampled ground
// height, not a guess. CITY zones are the world's own Names entries that sit
// on dry land with at least 3 building(s) within 300 m - the same test the
// running engine applies (ZoneRegistry::LandscapeSettlementProbe).
//
// BEFORE YOU SHIP THIS, by hand:
//   1. defaultOccupier / defaultResistance below are PLACEHOLDERS. Set them to
//      CfgGuerrillaFactions class names your data set actually ships (the global
//      library is guerrilla-mode/config/guerrilla-factions.hpp; a mod may add
//      its own). playerSide must be the side the mission.sqm player is welded
//      to - the engine counts resistance presence through that side's center.
//   2. Walk the Camp and the Outposts in the editor. The placement rules know
//      about roads, water and slope; they know nothing about fences, compounds
//      or minefields, so a spot can be legal and still be walled in.
//   3. Rename the Outposts to real places and tune garrison / income.
//   4. Add a CfgGuerrillaMarket block if this island should have dealers.

onLoadMission = "Guerrilla Mode - Everon";
onLoadIntro  = "Liberate Everon, one zone at a time.";
respawn = 0;
joinInProgress = 0;

